<% title "Privacy Policy" %>
<section class="md-section">
  <div class="md-section__inner md-stack">
    <p class="md-section__eyebrow">PokéMart</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Test-only demo — not a live store.</strong> This policy describes what the PokéMart demo collects. It is intentionally minimal because the demo stores almost nothing.</p>
    <h2>1. Data we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>Email address</strong> — collected at demo checkout solely to deliver the signed receipt link and to display your order. <strong>Session data</strong> — your shopping cart is kept in your browser session (a server-side session cookie), not in a database tied to you. <strong>Basic request logs</strong> — standard web server logs (IP, user agent, timestamps) for operation and abuse prevention.</p>
    <h2>2. How we use it</h2>
    <p>To run the demo: keep your cart, complete the simulated checkout, email your receipt link, and keep the service stable. We do not sell, rent, or share personal data with third parties for marketing.</p>
    <h2>3. Payments</h2>
    <p>None. The demo uses a local test simulator — no payment processor, no card data, no billing information.</p>
    <h2>4. Retention and your choices</h2>
    <p>Session carts expire with your session. Demo orders and emails are retained only as long as the demo environment exists (the hosted preview wipes daily at 3AM Mexico City). You may ask for your data to be deleted at any time by contacting us below.</p>
    <h2>5. Operator details</h2>
    <p>Until a named legal entity, address, and monitored mailbox are provided, this demo is explicitly test-only and no production claims are made about data handling.</p>
    <h2>6. Contact</h2>
    <p>Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:legal@pokemart.api.holode.xyz">legal@pokemart.api.holode.xyz</a>.</p>
    <p><em>Version 1.0 — August 2026.</em></p>
  </div>
</section>
